From: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 03:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: enable Android data compatibility algorithms on Nabu

Android userdata from older and newer platform generations may use Adiantum
or HCTR2 even though Nabu's Android 16 profile normally uses AES-XTS and
AES-CTS. Build both algorithms as modules so the data bridge can cover the
full Android 9-17 compatibility matrix without increasing the boot-critical
kernel image.

Signed-off-by: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
---
 senemos/configs/nabu-minimal.config | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/senemos/configs/nabu-minimal.config b/senemos/configs/nabu-minimal.config
index b120fbf9f..8a9780d5a 100644
--- a/senemos/configs/nabu-minimal.config
+++ b/senemos/configs/nabu-minimal.config
@@ -40,6 +40,9 @@ CONFIG_DM_DEFAULT_KEY=y
 CONFIG_FS_ENCRYPTION=y
 CONFIG_FS_ENCRYPTION_ALGS=y
 CONFIG_FS_ENCRYPTION_INLINE_CRYPT=y
+# Android 9-17 userdata compatibility beyond Nabu's normal AES-XTS/CTS path.
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_ADIANTUM=m
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_HCTR2=m
 CONFIG_F2FS_FS=m
 CONFIG_F2FS_FS_XATTR=y
 CONFIG_F2FS_FS_POSIX_ACL=y
-- 
2.55.0
